# Large re-downloadable reference database (auto-fetched by
# notebooks/accuracy_fixed_executed.ipynb from ftp.ebi.ac.uk if missing; ~323MB,
# exceeds GitHub's single-file limit and shouldn't live in git history)
datasets/hla.dat

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Debug/run logs from one-off script invocations, anywhere in the repo.
*.log

# Scratch/debug artifacts named by convention, not meant to be permanent:
# a leading underscore marks a one-off working file (e.g. _run_poster.log,
# _old_pre_rewrite/), and "URGENT_*" marks an ad-hoc cross-check dumped
# during active debugging -- several already-committed URGENT_* files
# reference the "filtered/unfiltered" scoring split retired 2026-10-18 and
# are now actively stale, not just unpolished.
URGENT_*
_old_pre_*/
notebooks/_old_pre_novel_removal/

# Raw sequencing data / aligner indices / per-run logs (hundreds of GB;
# re-derivable from datasets/raw/*.sh scripts + public accessions, never
# meant to live in git). A handful of small pre-existing files under
# datasets/raw/ predate this rule and stay tracked (git already has them);
# everything else new under here is ignored.
datasets/raw/*_bams/
datasets/raw/*_fastq_tmp/
datasets/raw/d8_pacbio/
datasets/raw/star_index/
datasets/raw/references/
datasets/raw/hlapers_ref/
datasets/raw/hlapers_hladb/
datasets/raw/hlapers_index.idx
datasets/raw/t1k_ref/
datasets/raw/d1_*/
datasets/raw/d2_*/
datasets/raw/d4_*/
datasets/raw/d7_*/
datasets/raw/d8_*/
datasets/raw/phlat_index_build/

# Deliberate pre-fix/pre-refresh backups (project convention: kept on disk,
# never committed -- see .claude/memory/KNOWN_BUGS.md for what each one is a
# backup of).
*.bak
*.bak_*
*_backup/

# Sibling working directories that now live inside the repo root after
# flattening repo/ up a level (2026-10-08) -- never meant to be tracked.
/tools/
/.venv/

# Local Claude Code settings -- purged from git history 2026-10-08; never
# meant to be tracked (per-machine config, not project state).
/.claude/

# Internal/process documentation -- not for publication (Human-PI decision,
# 2026-10-22). Only a file literally named README.md (any directory) and the
# top-level LICENSE are exempt -- everything else written in Markdown stays
# local. Previously-tracked instances were purged from git history + force-
# pushed the same day; this prevents any of them (or new ones) from being
# re-added by a future `git add -A` / `git add .`.
*.md
!**/README.md

# Headline per-tool accuracy numbers -- same "not for publication ahead of
# the manuscript" reasoning as the Markdown rule above, just in csv/json
# instead of .md (Human-PI decision, 2026-10-22). Purged from git history +
# force-pushed the same day; kept on local disk.
/verification/

# archives of raw data/indices (e.g. the PHLAT index zip shared via Google Drive)
datasets/raw/*.zip
